WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.650
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.700
but also in crime.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.370
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.540
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:49.230
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:53.990
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.330
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:07.670
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.210
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:19.720
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:23.850
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.690
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:32.900
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.150
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:42.370
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:47.790
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.130
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.300
Noa's Big Adventure

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.810
Police School
Okutama Branch

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:20.910
This time, Izumi, you'll find
I'm not such an easy target!

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.200
Remember, Noa, Ota's
only good for a blind rush.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:28.620
Just step out of his way.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.420
Got it.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.340
Side punch!

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.010
What are you doing?

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.760
Moving like that will
burst your actuator!

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:46.470
Shut up! When you're in a
fight you have to improvise!

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.930
It's only a practice session.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.060
Now you've done it!

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.440
How dare you!

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.450
Hello, Shinobu.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.070
No, we're only
staying seven days.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:08.000
Keep things under
control until then. Bye.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:09.910
Hey, Goto.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:15.960
This is pathetic. Are you going to let
every session deteriorate like this?

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.130
It's realistic.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.510
I give up!

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.310
If you keep abusing
the Ingrams like this...

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.940
we'll never get
good measurements.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:35.860
Measurements?

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.240
Movements and stresses
under controlled conditions.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.490
Isn't it enough that the
Ingram can do what it does?

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.540
How can the son of a
great entrepreneur ask that?

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.460
The boss would cry
if he heard such talk.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.040
Cry?
My father?

00:03:54.540 --> 00:04:02.130
By learning from the Ingrams,
we can craft the next generation.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:08.510
And you used them so brilliantly
at Haruumi and the Castle Gate.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.930
My men were very impressed.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.280
Oh, no!
He's scratched here, too!

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.280
He's scratched all over!

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:27.490
Par for the course in
hand-to-hand combat!

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:32.540
You should cry less
and practice more!

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.550
What's wrong?
What's the big sigh for?

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.680
Nothing. Ota moved better
than I expected him to.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:46.890
Is that all?

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.100
That's all.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:14.080
I'm all bruised.
And after training so hard!

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:19.590
Maybe I'm no good after all.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.710
I wish I could see
some positive results.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:44.990
There!

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:45.860
Hey...

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.280
I think you hit it.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.870
Asuma, how'd I do?

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:51.990
See for yourself.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.040
I'd rather have you tell me.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.380
All of them hit the target!

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.510
Or the board.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.630
I never even practice,
and I'm still pretty good!

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.970
Then why don't you
use your gun more?

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.180
This cannon, inside city limits?

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.390
It might be useful,
once in a while.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.100
Then this is good enough.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.900
I can't understand her.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.110
What?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.440
She's mad when her
machine gets a scratch.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:29.030
The gun would cut down on
her hand-to-hand combat.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.820
It could be worse.
Ota's too eager to shoot.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:37.200
He wastes ammo, so he needs
hand-to-hand for a fallback.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.670
More bullets!

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:48.510
Those cartridges are expensive!
You need to pace yourself!

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:54.010
But I need more bullets,
or this practice is pointless!

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:56.390
We didn't requisition
very many...

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.430
You done?

00:06:58.850 --> 00:06:59.640
Let's see...

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.020
Well?

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:07.030
Maybe Izumi is correct to avoid guns.
Her accuracy is terrible.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:14.950
Well if Ota's so great, why doesn't
he hit the target more often?

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.240
Actually...

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:17.870
Take a look.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.790
He may not hit his opponent's
head, but he's pretty good.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.670
Then why does
he miss so often?

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:33.640
It's hard to hit a moving
target, especially a limb.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.760
This is boring. Next!

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.400
For a second, I thought I
might be a natural marksman.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.700
Miss Izumi, what
are you doing here?

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:56.660
Oh, Hiromi.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.910
You don't look very happy.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.540
Oh, it's nothing.
What about you, Hiromi?

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:05.830
Aren't you lonely,
taking classes by yourself?

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:13.130
No. Since I can't train as a pilot,
I'm learning emergency repairs.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:18.260
Now I'll be able to help out
if you get damaged in a fight.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.140
It sounds like fun!

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.020
Well, they said I
have a knack for it.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.730
Oh. Congratulations.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.530
What's wrong?

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.660
Let me show you again.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.790
I can't pick it up instantly.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:45.040
I didn't grow up with
computers like you, Asuma.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:46.830
Why are you sulking?

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:51.840
I'd like to continue,
but I need dinner, first.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.300
Maybe the restaurant
downhill is still open.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.090
Let's draw straws.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:57.930
No.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.640
I'll go.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.110
Thirty miles per hour
over the speed limit!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.470
Could it be?
Babylon! Babylon!

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:44.470
I knew it!

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:59.410
20,000 yen! I can see movies,
eat fine food, play Patlabor!

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.290
What am I talking about!
Get going!

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.500
And I'm off!

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.260
What's keeping Noa?

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:28.600
I was hoping she'd be back
before Ota got out of the bath.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.980
Here comes Ota!

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.320
Where's Noa?

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.740
Ah, nice bath.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.380
This...

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.810
This smells like a case!

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.730
Is Izumi here or not?
Answer me!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:14.560
Calm down!

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.030
Where'd she go at
this hour, Asuma?

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:20.990
Well, we were hungry.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:29.830
She's AWOL! It's a blatant
disregard for regulations!

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.120
We know! Don't shout!

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.340
What's going on?

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:44.300
There was a robbery in Itabashi,
and the suspect fled this way.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.390
We think he's heading
into the mountains.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.200
It's that car I saw.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:14.880
Danger

00:12:56.830 --> 00:13:00.130
That idiot!
She's following the trail upstream?

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.840
What if she finds the burglar?

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:03.670
Captain Goto.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:12.100
HQ is calling.
There's no need for a dragnet -

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:16.350
I get it! Just because
Second Section is on hand...

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.520
we're shanghaied
into catching criminals.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.610
Good thing you're
always so prepared.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.950
Izumi's an idiot, but
she's also a colleague.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.620
Isao Ota will give her attacker
the clenched fist of justice!

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.370
What a nice guy.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.490
Or at least, not a bad guy.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:39.500
What's with Noa? She isn't
the type to run off on her own.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:43.210
Noa's been acting
kind of strange today.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.140
Ouch.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:54.640
Help me!

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:01.650
Don't be scared.
I won't hurt you.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.860
We're splitting into groups.
Ota, follow the river upstream.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.320
Shinohara and Yamazaki,
take the radio and go with him.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.240
I have to go with this lunkhead?

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.790
Who's a lunkhead?

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:17.250
Shinshi, you're with me.
We'll look for Izumi's bike.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:18.670
Well, let's move, people!

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:29.970
Let's go.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.640
I know!
You don't have to say it!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.100
Ouch.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.650
I offered to carry your bag.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:45.070
No, never!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:46.690
Anything but that!

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:48.610
Suspicious.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.950
Promise not to tell the
police about my money!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.830
I can't do that.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.990
How can you be so cruel?

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.830
I've got it!

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:01.330
Wait right here!

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.710
What if I give you this?

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:09.170
What's that?

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:10.970
You can have more,
if you keep quiet!

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.800
Don't be an idiot.
Let's go.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.020
Okay, how about TWO stacks?

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:18.680
What's that?

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.940
I found it in the river. It fell out
of your bag, so I'm returning it.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:27.400
Kids these days are so uptight!

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:32.240
How could Izumi
run off like this?

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:35.740
We were so close by!

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.870
She should have called us
when she spotted the cash!

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:42.120
That undisciplined upstart!

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:43.960
Fine, just keep moving.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.920
I'm only going to say this once!

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:50.380
If those criminals hurt Izumi,
I'll beat them to a pulp!

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:03.400
Are you sure you can't keep
quiet about the money?

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.440
I told you, I can't do that.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:09.570
And there are bills in the river.
I'm sure the police are coming.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.360
You could say you don't
know where they came from.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.280
But I DO know.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:19.870
You're so stubborn!
You're as pigheaded as a cop!

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:21.120
I AM a cop.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:24.620
Who?

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:25.330
Me.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:26.630
No!

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:27.380
Yes.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.260
This is terrible!

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.630
Money doesn't look so fine
when you need to hide it.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.470
And what a waste -

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:37.800
Izumi!

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:40.180
Get away from him!
He's a burglar!

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:41.770
Burglar?

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:46.650
I'm no burglar!

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:50.860
Enough! That ill-gotten booty
under your arm is proof enough!

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.610
Captain, we've found Izumi.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.950
Yes, thank you.
I can see that.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:02.200
So how do you
explain all this cash?

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.910
Ota, don't be so rough!

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:08.000
This guy says
he isn't a burglar!

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.250
That's true.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:12.130
Yeah, you burglars are all alike!

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:16.220
What?

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:22.560
They've already captured the burglar.
Didn't I mention that?

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:29.810
Captain, we'd appreciate it if
you wouldn't treat us so flippantly.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:31.020
Sorry.

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:34.440
We were really
worried about Noa.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:39.370
Fool! I was simply focused
on capturing the criminal.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.700
I could have cared less
what happened to Izumi.

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:45.160
I quote: "If those criminals hurt
Izumi, I'll beat them to a pulp!"

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:49.790
Oh, that! I'm just concerned
about my colleagues.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.710
That was a perfectly
acceptable remark.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.050
Right, Captain?

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.930
Why are you blushing?

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:00.300
I don't get it.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:05.930
This whole mess is your fault!
Don't you understand that?

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.520
What's that about?

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:15.610
All that pressure had
to come out somehow.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:17.820
Officer's room

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:20.200
You know how to handle
the paperwork, don't you?

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.790
Turn it in tomorrow.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:25.790
Uh...

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:27.290
What?

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.580
Aren't you going
to reprimand me?

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:30.540
Oh, yeah.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.800
Try not to get in trouble
out of sight of your backup.

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:38.720
That's all.

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:40.970
Yes, sir.
Thank you, sir.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.650
You must be cold.
Go take a hot bath.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:54.020
Thanks.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:59.150
Shinohara?

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.450
Did she say anything?

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.320
About what?

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:07.120
About tonight! She isn't the
type to run off on her own.

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.120
I agree.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:14.380
I'd expect her to run back yelling,
"I found money in the river!"

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:18.340
So do you have any idea why
she acted the way she did?

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.220
Well... I have a suspicion.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:24.220
I heard there was 50
million yen in that bag.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:29.480
We <i>should</i> be suspicious of
anyone carrying a wad like that!

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:33.440
Maybe he was hiding
laundered money, and he slipped.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.570
It's been three minutes.

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:38.740
I think you're right.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.400
Yeah.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:45.580
Well, I can't help. Anything I said
would be taken as an order.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.660
YOU do the counseling.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.120
Me?

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:54.080
She's your partner. This should
come from the command car.

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:58.050
Can I ask you one question?

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:02.510
Do you really think that everyone
in Division 2 is in the right post?

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.840
I don't have to answer that.

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:09.600
Do I look like I'd make
a mistake like that?

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:16.230
Why did you want to see me?

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:19.980
When you saw that 10,000
yen bill in the river...

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.070
you knew it was
a case, didn't you?

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:26.530
Didn't you think
about alerting us?

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:35.500
How can I explain it?
I had to find the source right away.

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.750
I'll try to be more
careful next time.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.590
You weren't trying
to prove yourself?

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.720
What makes you think that?

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:48.390
Long ago at school, there was a
benchwarmer for the rugby team.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:51.850
One game, he got his big chance.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:57.480
The ball was passed to him,
and the field was totally clear.

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:03.780
He thought, "I'm clear!"
He never thought of passing.

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:08.660
He ran and ran, but inches
from the goal, he was tackled.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:14.410
His team won, but he went
back to being a benchwarmer.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.250
Nice try, kid.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:18.670
And that was you?

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:21.880
It's the story of someone
who misjudged the situation.

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:27.760
Well, maybe I was looking
for a little recognition...

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:30.760
but you're all so
much better than I am.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:35.270
"Everyone is in the proper post in
Division 2." The Captain said so.

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:40.690
You proved it, when you
fought the Black Labor.

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:43.190
You do plenty.

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:45.150
Maybe you're right.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:49.990
Believe in yourself.
Make the best of what you've got.

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:55.660
Asuma...

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:02.210
She's back!
She's back!

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:04.590
Who's going to do it?

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:06.470
Do what?

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:10.680
It should be Ota.
After all, he's her teammate.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:12.100
You're right.

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:14.310
What?
What?

00:22:14.310 --> 00:22:15.850
Presentation of the bouquet.

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:18.560
Forget it!

00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:20.480
Quit whining!

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:22.520
Yamazaki, you do it!

00:22:23.190 --> 00:22:24.940
What, me?

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:29.110
Good morning,
everyone! I'm back.

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:34.910
Do it right, bozo!

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.290
Congratulations on
your full recovery.

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:39.960
Thank you.

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:04.860
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:12.620
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:14.580
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:20.040
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:28.340
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:30.590
I got it

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:38.140
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:44.020
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:45.570
One more chance

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:53.200
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:58.660
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:02.330
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:11.840
This story is fiction...

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:11.840
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:17.510 --> 00:24:19.220
If you destroy
something, it's OK!

00:24:19.220 --> 00:24:20.930
You're insured!

00:24:20.930 --> 00:24:23.900
But when you destroy property you
have to fill out LOTS of paperwork!

00:24:23.900 --> 00:24:25.810
The insurance company has
sent an agent to watch over us...

00:24:25.810 --> 00:24:27.400
because we've caused
SO MUCH damage!

00:24:27.650 --> 00:24:29.650
There's a limit to how
much you can control!

00:24:29.650 --> 00:24:36.070
We really tried to do our
best in front of the agent!

00:24:36.070 --> 00:24:40.080
Next Time: I'm Selling Peace of Mind.
Target, locked on!

00:24:39.330 --> 00:24:44.330
Next episode

00:24:39.330 --> 00:24:44.330
I’m Selling Peace of Mind
